review_text:
Update: I emailed their company, told them my problem, they answered lighting fast, less than an hour, after trying their fix, it worked. 

Now I can say the game is awesome again, sad as ♥♥♥ maybe, sure, but im loving it.

what happened: my guy died, i was heartbroken so i tried to close the game with task manage 
hoping it wouldnt save. it seems that doing so corrupted the save file and now the game would crash on startup. Basically had to erase the save file while offline and that fixed it, heres their email for reference. the second option is what worked.

- make sure that Steam is in offline mode (this will prevent the game from downloading the broken save from the Steam Cloud);
- go to folder: (wherever you have Steam Installed)\Steam\userdata\YOUR-PROFILE-ID-NUMBER\282070\remote (For me it's C:\Apps\Steam\userdata\7XXXXX1\282070\remote);
- delete/rename/move the "savedgames" file;
- change the "savedgames.alt" file name to "savedgames";
- launch the game and click "continue";
- your game should load the state from the previous day.

If this fails as well, please go to the folder at "%appdata%/11bitstudios/This War of Mine" (you can simply copy the directory and paste it into the adress bar in Explorer) and delete the "iPhoneProfiles" file. This is the file that records beginning and end of each session - the end of session is recorded when the game is closed via choosing the appropriate option from the menu in-game, and unexpected shutdown of the game may cause the session end not to be recorded, which leads to an error within Steam upon next launch. Please delete the file and try to launch the game again.

Good things : 
-incredible visual effects;
-great animation;
-good narrative and story;
-gameplay is easy but takes time to do things so you got be patient;
____________________________________________
Bad things :
-you start the game with no clue or tutorial about the gameplay;
-no tip or hint about the icons and you have to interact everytime to learn about them;
-the game is built in a permanent saving progress. If something go wrong along the time, you better be prepare about the consequences;
-you can't bind the keyboard to move the camera, only mouse;
-font size is unbelievable squeezed no matter what resolution set you change, the font size will be the same as much as hard is to read;

My Friend Buy Me This Game When Aumtum Sale.
I Feel Sad When Start Scavenging The Quiet House And Seeing The Couple Who Live In There So Helpless ;-;
Very Well Done 11 Bit Studio This Game Is 100% Recommended To Play

Beautiful and peaceful game. Little bit overwhelming at first (what to do) but once you get the hang of how to surive it becomes fun and makes you think about the strategic and ethic decisions you can make.

+ Interesting story: scavenge to survive with ethical choices;
+ Multiple strategies: grab/steal what you can or produce and trade;
+ Well chosen and peaceful audio/soundtracks;
+ Variance in gameplay: different locations, characters, changing weather, radio news;
+ Beautiful graphics and styling;
- User created workshops have compatibility problems due game updates;
- Some game bugs (one crash to desktop, one time unable to move a character anymore).

[h1]This War of Mine[/h1]

A must-buy for anyone who's even remotely interested in strategy and/or good video games. At first I was a bit overwhelmed by the different elements of the game, and this affected my first play-through to the point where failing made me feel genuinely sad. Not because I didn't "win", but rather because of the unjustness of the conditions that caused my survivors to get sick or depressed and eventually die. And after 30 or so hours and getting better at the game, I started wondering if that might have been the point: everything doesn't neatly fall into place for civilians in wartime—death is constant. And maybe that's what this game teaches: yes, as you play, things start to feel more and more enjoyable, so to speak, but first you have to go through a harsher, more honest representation of war.

[b]Pros:[/b]
[list]
[*]Beautiful artwork, tense atmosphere;
[*]Tackles important themes in a surprisingly harsh but honest light;
[*]Decent amount of locations to explore, along with new characters and simply getting used to the mechanics adds to replayability;
[*]Decisions have tangible consequences;
[*]Gameplay adapts to your play style;
[*]Great soundtrack;
[/list]

[b]Cons:[/b]
[list]
[*]Lack of tutorial can make things a bit overwhelming (if not downright depressing) at first;
[*]Not a lot of [i]scenario[/i] variations to increase replay value, in contrast to the above.
[/list]

reccomending this as an artwork, not gameplay (to be honest, the gameplay mechanics get very rote, not a game in the traditional sense)

Having to rob an elderly couple for bandages, I hoped they would pull out a weapon and shoot. They only begged the character to stop, then right before exiting, the old man said "How will we survive the winter now?" 

;_;

amazing game, it catches you emotionally! It's a very immersive experience for many reasons : 
- graphic style is perfectly chosen; 
- needs of characters; 
- reactions of characters to the events;
- hard decisions to take in difficult moments;
- etc etc etc... 

I can't stop to play it!
